  "full_text": "There's a person in the streets that's practically dying, and he's cold, and they're covering him up. And one of the locals went over there and said, yeah, he's kind of bent over to try and help him and stuff. And I can't really do anything. I don't really have any resources. So the good thing is, if you don't have any resources, you don't really have any responsibility. If you do have resources, you have responsibility. So basically, if I can't save anybody because I don't have any resources, that's not my fault. So it's not my guilt. But those who have resources, they'll be judged. So anyway, you know, maybe they're supposed to let him die. I don't know. But maybe they're supposed to not let him die. You know, so anyway.",
